  "grammar": [
    {"title": "不如…啦 = how about…",
     "explain": "Start with 不如 and end with 啦 to make a friendly suggestion. To accept: 好啊 / 好主意; to decline politely: 唔得啊，我約咗人.",
     "examples": [
       {"en": "How about meeting at the MTR station?", "parts": [["不如","bat1 jyu4"],["喺","hai2"],["地鐵站","dei6 tit3 zaam6"],["等","dang2"],["啦","laa1"],["。"]]},
       {"en": "How about we reschedule to Sunday?", "parts": [["不如","bat1 jyu4"],["改期","goi2 kei4"],["去","heoi3"],["星期日","sing1 kei4 jat6"],["啦","laa1"],["。"]]}
     ]},
    {"title": "Time + place + verb",
     "explain": "Cantonese order is fixed: who → when → where → what. 我哋 + 七點 + 喺門口 + 等.",
